<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Skanderbeg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1405">1405</a>–<a href="/years/1468">1468</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Gjergj Kastrioti</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Skanderbeg, born Gjergj Kastrioti, was an Albanian lord who served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and in 1443 broke with them and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kruje">Krujë</a>. In 1444 he formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-lezhe">League of Lezhë</a> with other Albanian nobles and for twenty-five years resisted Ottoman campaigns, including sieges of Krujë. Albania fell to the Ottomans within a decade of his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/skanderbeg.jpg" alt="Skanderbeg" width="320" height="331" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Skanderbeg_(1466).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
